{"name":"Reflecting Pond","hex":"#234251","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"reflecting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of reflect"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of reflection (in any sense)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reflecting"},{"term":"pond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inland body of standing water, either natural or man-made, that is smaller than a lake.","An inland body of standing water of any size that is fed by springs rather than by a river."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Chiefly in across the pond: the Atlantic Ocean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Reflecting pool","blocks":[{"text":"A reflecting pool, also called a reflection pool, is a water feature found in gardens, parks and memorial sites. It usually consists of a shallow pool of water with a reflective surface, undisturbed by fountain jets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Madrid-Debod-TempleP1340709.jpg/330px-Madrid-Debod-TempleP1340709.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflecting_pool"},{"title":"Pond","blocks":[{"text":"A pond is a small, still, land-based body of water formed by pooling inside a depression, either naturally or artificially. A pond is smaller than a lake and there are no official criteria distinguishing the two, although defining a pond to be less than 5 hectares in area, less than 5 metres (16 ft) in depth and with less than 30% of its area covered by emergent vegetation helps in distinguishing the ecology of ponds from those of lakes and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg/330px-Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w